title: Hungary
subtitle: Choose between democratic ties, state business and the PiS–Fidesz axis.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 95
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and year >= 2022 and poland_european_right_timer <= 0
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_european_right_timer = 5; foreign_cards_resolved += 1; foreign_authority_last_issue = "Hungary"
card-image: img/poland/cards/national-left-rally.webp

= Hungary

**Government in Budapest:** [+ hungary_government +].
**2022 result:** [+ hungary_election_2022_result +].
**2026 result:** [+ hungary_election_2026_result +].
Hungary relationship **[+ hungary_relation +]/100** · democratic network
**[+ hungary_democratic_network +]/100** · Fidesz channel **[+
hungary_fidesz_channel +]/100**.

PiS treats Orbán's Hungary as proof that a conservative government can resist
EU pressure with a friendly neighbour beside it. Lewica can talk to the
Hungarian opposition and civil society without pretending it represents the
Polish state; a Polish cabinet must also keep practical business moving.

- @democrats
- @state
- @fidesz

@democrats
title: [? if not left_in_government: Connect the Polish opposition to Hungarian democrats and election monitors?][? if left_in_government: Put democratic standards and civil society into the bilateral relationship?]
subtitle: Builds a channel that can survive Fidesz—and modestly improves the chance of a democratic change.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
Q.hungary_democratic_network += executive ? 7 : 6;
Q.eu_institutional_trust += executive ? 3 : 2;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
if (Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power) {
    Q.hungary_relation -= executive ? 3 : 1;
}
if (executive) {
    Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 2;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Poland keeps state contact while funding transparent democratic exchange";
} else {
    Q.media_capacity += 1;
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Opposition international network";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Lewica and Hungarian democratic organisations";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome =
        "Opposition links evidence, observers and democratic parties across the border";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

The network is built with people who may never govern, which is exactly why it
survives whoever does. Budapest calls it interference; the Hungarian
organisations on the other end are the only reason the friction is worth it.

- #poland_card_finish

@state
title: [? if hungary_fidesz_in_power = 1: Keep a narrow working channel with Orbán's government?][? if hungary_fidesz_in_power = 0: Reset relations with the new Tisza government?]
subtitle: Practical diplomacy without endorsing the governing party.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
Q.hungary_relation += executive ? 6 : 3;
if (Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power) {
    Q.eu_institutional_trust -= executive ? 2 : 1;
    Q.ukraine_solidarity -= 1;
} else {
    Q.eu_institutional_trust += executive ? 4 : 2;
    Q.ukraine_solidarity += 2;
}
if (executive) {
    Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 2;
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome = Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power
        ? "Cabinet keeps disputes with Budapest inside a narrow working channel"
        : "Cabinet opens a democratic reset with the Tisza government";
} else {
    Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome = Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power
        ? "Lewica maintains party-level contact without speaking for Poland"
        : "Lewica turns its opposition network into access to the new government";
}
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

States talk to states. Keeping the channel narrow and practical means neither
pretending the neighbouring government is normal nor letting the border, the
freight and the interconnector become hostages to the argument about it.

- #poland_card_finish

@fidesz
title: Join PiS in cultivating the Fidesz axis
subtitle: Easier conservative access; worse EU trust and Ukraine solidarity.
on-arrival: {!
const executive = Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government;
Q.hungary_fidesz_channel += executive ? 8 : 6;
Q.hungary_relation += Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power ? 5 : -2;
Q.pis_relation += 5;
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.eu_institutional_trust -= executive ? 6 : 3;
Q.ukraine_solidarity -= 3;
Q.foreign_pressure += 2;
if (executive) Q.foreign_policy_responsibility += 5;
Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome = Q.hungary_fidesz_in_power
    ? "Lewica borrows the PiS–Fidesz channel and inherits its conflicts"
    : "Lewica stays with Fidesz after Hungarian voters remove it from government";
Q.news_headline = Q.foreign_authority_last_outcome;
!}

The channel arrives with its owners. Lewica gains conservative access it did
not build and inherits every quarrel attached to it, and the progressive wing
has to be told why the Left is keeping a seat warm for PiS.

- #poland_card_finish
